  "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the ${x}^{2}$ and $x$ terms. So, we first rewrite it by including the missing terms with a coefficient of zero, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}-1={x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-1\n$$\n\nNow, using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+2x-1 \\\\  & {x}^{2}+1\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+0x-1\\,\\,\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{4}+0{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2{x}^{3}-{x}^{2}+0x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{2{x}^{3}+0{x}^{2}+2x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,-{x}^{2}-2x-1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-{x}^{2}+0x-1}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,-2x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is ${x}^{2}+2x-1,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-2x.$",
